1329:    /// @dev Returns current price of an NFT on auction. Broken into two
1330:    ///  functions (this one, that computes the duration from the auction
1331:    ///  structure, and the other that does the price computation) so we
1332:    ///  can easily test that the price computation works correctly.
1333:    function _currentPrice(Auction storage _auction)
1334:        internal
1335:        view
1336:        returns (uint256)
1337:    {
1338:        uint256 secondsPassed = 0;
1339:
1340:        // A bit of insurance against negative values (or wraparound).
1341:        // Probably not necessary (since Ethereum guarnatees that the
1342:        // now variable doesn't ever go backwards).
1343:        if (now > _auction.startedAt) {
1344:            secondsPassed = now - _auction.startedAt;
1345:        }
1346:
1347:        return _computeCurrentPrice(
1348:            _auction.startingPrice,
1349:            _auction.endingPrice,
1350:            _auction.duration,
1351:            secondsPassed
1352:        );
